# Public copy

Public pages describe the chapter as it is now. Do not publish process copy, status notes, or site housekeeping.

That includes:

- How or when the site will be updated
- “Check back soon,” “will be added,” “as they are confirmed,” “until then”
- Notes about missing emails, photos, partners, or other unpublished details
- Internal work such as domain mapping, reviews still to do, or officer handoff

If a list is empty, use a short present-tense fact (`No upcoming events are listed.`) or omit the section. Do not explain that content is coming later.

Maintenance notes belong in `docs/` or YAML comments, not in `src/pages/` or visitor-facing components.
